<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  GIZKA_TRIBBLE_ADAPTATION_1 — patches against the DONOR gizka.

  The creature belongs to Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)
  (`Mlie.StarWarsAnimalCollection`, WS 3497316713). We never edit that mod;
  everything here is an xpath patch from our own mod, wrapped in
  PatchOperationFindMod so the whole file no-ops cleanly when the donor is
  absent.

  TWO separate owner rulings live in this file, and they pull in opposite
  directions on purpose:

  1. Card 2 (sitting 2026-09-12) — "~15 silver". The donor ships
     MarketValue 100. A swarm of hundred-silver animals is a money printer,
     which is exactly the ladder the anti-exponential law forbids. Flattened
     to 15: the KotOR scam stays funny, never income.

  2. Owner, 2026-09-17, verbatim: "But also ensure that the gizka creature
     itself does have that crazy reproduction rate everywhere in the world."
     The tribble-grade breeding is a property of the CREATURE, wherever one
     exists — wild, bought, traded, farmed — not something the stowaway event
     confers. So the donor's own reproduction numbers are patched here, and
     the event is only one delivery vector among several.

  Which numbers are the real reproduction knobs: gizka is an EGG LAYER
  (CompProperties_EggLayer on the donor def), so it never runs the live-birth
  path at all. `RaceProperties.gestationPeriodDays` (-1 default) and
  `RaceProperties.litterSizeCurve` (null default) are both unset on the donor
  and are INERT for this creature — PawnUtility.Mated() routes an egg-layer
  female to CompEggLayer.Fertilize(male) and never to Hediff_Pregnant. Setting
  them would change nothing and would read as a fact that was never true.
  The chain that actually governs gizka population growth is:

      mate (mateMtbHours) -> fertilize (eggFertilizationCountMax clutches)
      -> lay (eggLayIntervalDays x eggCountRange)
      -> hatch (EggGizkaFertilized hatcherDaystoHatch)
      -> mature (lifeStageAges minAge)  -> mate again

  Every link in that chain is shortened below. Values are MEASURED from the
  donor's own XML (1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Races_Animal_SW.xml and
  1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_swanimal_Items.xml), before -> after:

      MarketValue                 100    -> 15      (Card 2, not breeding)
      eggLayIntervalDays          1      -> 0.4
      eggCountRange               1~2    -> 3~5
      eggFertilizationCountMax    1      -> 4
      mateMtbHours                (12, engine default; absent from the donor)
                                         -> 4
      hatcherDaystoHatch          4      -> 1.5     (EggGizkaFertilized)
      lifeStageAges AnimalJuvenile minAge 0.04 (~14.6 d) -> 0.02 (~7.3 d)
      lifeStageAges AnimalAdult    minAge 0.09 (~32.9 d) -> 0.045 (~16.4 d)

  (minAge is in YEARS of a 60-day RimWorld year, so 0.09 yr = 5.4 days only
  at the 60-day figure quoted in the draft; the engine's year is 3,600,000
  ticks = 60 days, so 0.09 yr = 5.4 days and 0.045 yr = 2.7 days. Either way
  the halving is the change, not the absolute.)

  Mod Settings can multiply these further at runtime (RSW_GizkaSettings
  "Global gizka breeding rate" rewrites the live def fields from this patched
  baseline on startup and on every settings change) — this file is the
  shipped default, not a ceiling or a floor.

  NOT patched, deliberately: `roamMtbDays` (wild gizka still wander off, which
  is the only thing keeping a wild population from becoming a map-wide carpet),
  `wildBiomes` (the biome cast is SWBestiary's business, not ours), and the
  unfertilized egg's MarketValue 6 (a trickle, and the anti-exponential law
  only cares that it stays flat).
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- Card 2: the scam pays pocket change. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Gizka"]/statBases/MarketValue</xpath>
          <value>
            <MarketValue>15</MarketValue>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Owner 2026-09-17: crazy reproduction, everywhere. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Gizka"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_EggLayer"]/eggLayIntervalDays</xpath>
          <value>
            <eggLayIntervalDays>0.4</eggLayIntervalDays>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Gizka"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_EggLayer"]/eggCountRange</xpath>
          <value>
            <eggCountRange>3~5</eggCountRange>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Gizka"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_EggLayer"]/eggFertilizationCountMax</xpath>
          <value>
            <eggFertilizationCountMax>4</eggFertilizationCountMax>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- mateMtbHours is absent from the donor def, so this is an Add, not
             a Replace: RaceProperties defaults it to 12. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Gizka"]/race</xpath>
          <value>
            <mateMtbHours>4</mateMtbHours>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Gizka"]/race/lifeStageAges/li[def="AnimalJuvenile"]/minAge</xpath>
          <value>
            <minAge>0.02</minAge>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Gizka"]/race/lifeStageAges/li[def="AnimalAdult"]/minAge</xpath>
          <value>
            <minAge>0.045</minAge>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="EggGizkaFertilized"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_Hatcher"]/hatcherDaystoHatch</xpath>
          <value>
            <hatcherDaystoHatch>1.5</hatcherDaystoHatch>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    THE SECOND GIZKA. MEASURED 2026-09-17, and it is not in the draft.

    MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Pass 12 (commit 2cd0ebcb1, tonight) ported the
    donor's gizka into SWBestiary as `RSW_Gizka` + `RSW_EggGizkaFertilized` /
    `RSW_EggGizkaUnFertilized` — a defName rename only, every reproduction
    number carried across unchanged (MarketValue 100, eggLayIntervalDays 1,
    eggCountRange 1~2, eggFertilizationCountMax 1, hatcherDaystoHatch 4,
    AnimalJuvenile 0.04 / AnimalAdult 0.09). Both creatures are live at once
    today, and the absorption program exists so the donor can eventually be
    retired.

    The owner's ruling is about the CREATURE, not about one mod's copy of it.
    Patching only the donor would mean the crazy reproduction rate silently
    disappears on the day Star Wars Animal Collection is unsubscribed — the
    exact class of stale-by-construction change this repo keeps getting
    bitten by. So the same numbers are applied to the ported pair, by the
    same arithmetic.

    Keyed on the def's own presence (PatchOperationConditional) rather than on
    a mod NAME: PatchOperationFindMod matches ModLister.HasActiveModWithName,
    so a one-character drift in "RimMandrake: SW — Bestiary" would make this
    block stop applying without logging anything at all. A def-presence test
    cannot drift. It also returns true when it finds nothing, which is the
    graceful no-op wanted here and is deliberate, not an oversight.

    NOTE for whoever retires the donor: delete the FIRST operation block, not
    this one. Nothing else in this file needs to change.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]/statBases/MarketValue</xpath>
          <value>
            <MarketValue>15</MarketValue>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_EggLayer"]/eggLayIntervalDays</xpath>
          <value>
            <eggLayIntervalDays>0.4</eggLayIntervalDays>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_EggLayer"]/eggCountRange</xpath>
          <value>
            <eggCountRange>3~5</eggCountRange>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_EggLayer"]/eggFertilizationCountMax</xpath>
          <value>
            <eggFertilizationCountMax>4</eggFertilizationCountMax>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]/race</xpath>
          <value>
            <mateMtbHours>4</mateMtbHours>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]/race/lifeStageAges/li[def="AnimalJuvenile"]/minAge</xpath>
          <value>
            <minAge>0.02</minAge>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Gizka"]/race/lifeStageAges/li[def="AnimalAdult"]/minAge</xpath>
          <value>
            <minAge>0.045</minAge>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_EggGizkaFertilized"]/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_Hatcher"]/hatcherDaystoHatch</xpath>
          <value>
            <hatcherDaystoHatch>1.5</hatcherDaystoHatch>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
